        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{5x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | ${e}^{2}$ | ${e}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{5x\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|){|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613-\\operatorname{ln}\u20612) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
